<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Developer ID (direct-download DMG) build.

  Deliberately unsandboxed. App Sandbox is not required for Developer ID
  distribution, and the sandboxed entitlements in MythLog.entitlements — the App
  Group container and the iCloud ubiquity container — must be authorized by an
  embedded provisioning profile that only exists for App Store and Development
  channels. Signing those entitlements with a Developer ID certificate and no
  profile gets the binaries SIGKILLed on launch.

  Nothing is lost by dropping them here. AnchorDestination resolves iCloud
  anchors through the plain CloudDocs folder when unsandboxed
  (~/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/MythLog), and the ledger lives
  in ~/Library/Application Support/MythLog rather than a group container.

  MythLog.entitlements remains the App Store shape and is unchanged.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Hardened runtime is required for notarization. The AppleScript notification
	  fallback in Notifiers.swift spawns /usr/bin/osascript, which is only reachable
	  on the unsandboxed path — so it is live in this build and needs the Apple
	  Events exception it never needed in the sandboxed one.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
